  "description": "Apple Malus sp, classified by Landmark Trees as mature low quality (C) category 2 (landscape) with moderate vitality (marked with a grey dot as T in the sketch attached located in the rear garden of 23 Burstock road. I seek approval to fell the tree to ground level and replace it with a healthier tree in a better position. The proposal is based on the tree???s poor physiological quality, structural defects, and restrictive positioning. 1. Poor Physiological and Structural Quality: As shown in the attached photographs the main stem and primary upper canopy branches display a high density of significant canker-like burls, galls, and heavily distorted bark tissue. This systemic condition severely limits the long-term growth and aesthetic value. 2. Proximity to Built Structures: As shown in the photos attached the tree is situated in very close proximity to an adjacent brick building. 3. Low Public Amenity Value: Due to its species (domestic fruit tree), modest height (approx. 5m), and rear-garden location, the tree provides negligible public amenity value to the wider conservation area. Its removal will have no detrimental impact on the local landscape To maintain canopy cover within the conservation area I am proposing to plant a more appropriately sited replacement tree in the Position proposed on the attached sketch (PT).",
